### FD/EMFILE drill demo requests
### Start with: docker compose up --build
### Use scripts/demo.py for the full timing/echo assertions.

@api = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 1. API and echo process health
GET {{api}}/healthz

### 2. Initial status and RLIMIT_NOFILE
GET {{api}}/api/v1/status

### 3. Initial real accept(2) EMFILE counter
GET {{api}}/api/v1/metrics/emfile

### 3b. Optional one-request server-side full scenario
POST {{api}}/api/v1/drill/self-test

### 4. Fill the echo process descriptor table with retained sample logs
POST {{api}}/api/v1/drill/exhaust

### 5. While fault is active: old TCP connections still echo.
###    See scripts/demo.py for opening and verifying the long-lived connection.

### 6. API-side one-new-connection probe: expect outcome "eof" or "reset"
POST {{api}}/api/v1/probe
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "send_payload": false,
  "timeout_seconds": 1.0
}

### 7. Query actual EMFILE count during the fault
GET {{api}}/api/v1/metrics/emfile

### 8. Confirm accept thread is not burning CPU while idle in select()
GET {{api}}/api/v1/drill/accept-loop-check?seconds=1.0

### 9. Close sample log descriptors through the API
POST {{api}}/api/v1/drill/release

### 10. New connection must now echo
POST {{api}}/api/v1/probe
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "payload": "recovery-echo",
  "send_payload": true,
  "expect_echo": true,
  "timeout_seconds": 2.0
}

### Optional: open exactly N additional sample descriptors
POST {{api}}/api/v1/sample-files/open
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "count": 5
}

### Optional REST-style close
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/sample-files

### Optional restart of the managed echo process
POST {{api}}/api/v1/drill/restart
